                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s12IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#2v">-2v</locus>وَالْمُحْصَنَاتُ مِنَ النِّسآ إِلَّا مَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ<note>First word in red ink</note>
                     </incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#19r">-19r</locus>وَكَانَ اللهُ شَاكِراً عَلِيْماً</explicit>
                     <note>4:24-4:147. Fol. 2 is a replacement folio containing the beginning of ǧuz' 5. It is bound back to front, the text starting from fol. 2v. Fol. 19 is also a replacement folio, written by a different hand. Ihmāl marks (sīn). Deletions. On almost each folio, words rewritten or completed on the following line. Text enhanced (takbīr &amp; talwīn) on fol.10v (p. 19). Red triple dots as verse markers.</note>
                     <note/>
